From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pessi-v <pessimo@posteo.net>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 16:38:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] (lilac) dts: venus: drop the unresolvable smmu-vdd supply

msm_vidc's smmu-vdd-supply points at gdsc_bimc_smmu, which is disabled
on this board, so regulator lookup fails and enabling the regulators
dereferences NULL during boot. Without the property the driver gets a
dummy regulator and video encode/decode work.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-vidc.dtsi |    5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-vidc.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-vidc.dtsi
index b8d6134a96bb7aaec19caa709d696ca192cdf9a3..cd419649a365de6afd503f6a242f362bb36d9aec 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-vidc.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/msm8998-vidc.dtsi
@@ -72,7 +72,10 @@
 			<465000000 8490000>; /* imem @ turbo freq 406 Mhz */
 
 		/* Regulators */
-		smmu-vdd-supply = <&gdsc_bimc_smmu>;
+		/* lilac: no smmu-vdd-supply. gdsc_bimc_smmu is status="disabled" here as it
+		 * is on 4.4, and naming an unregistered provider makes this kernel return
+		 * -EPROBE_DEFER where 4.4 fell back to a dummy. Omitting it gives -ENODEV
+		 * -> dummy, i.e. exactly the rail Venus has always had on 4.4. */
 		venus-supply = <&gdsc_venus>;
 		venus-core0-supply = <&gdsc_venus_core0>;
 		venus-core1-supply = <&gdsc_venus_core1>;
